.TH XIL\-USE "1" "2026\-07\-02" "xil\-pipeline 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xil\-use \- set or display the active show context
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xil\-use
.br
.B xil\-use
\fI\,SHOW\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without arguments, lists all shows discovered in the current workspace (each
\fBconfigs/\fR\fI<slug>\fR\fB/project.json\fR) and marks the currently active show with
an asterisk.
.PP
With a show name or slug argument, switches the active show to that show.
Subsequent commands that auto\-detect the show (parse, produce, status, etc.)
will use the newly active show until changed again.
.PP
The active show is stored in \fI<workspace>\fR/.active_show.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I SHOW
Show name or slug to activate (e.g. \fB"Night Owls"\fR or \fBnightowls\fR).
Both forms are accepted.  Omit to list available shows.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
List all shows:
.B xil use
.TP
Switch to a show by name:
.B xil use "The Woonsocket Wonders"
.TP
Switch to a show by slug:
.B xil use thewoonsocketwonders
.TP
Via unified dispatcher:
.B xil use
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xil (1),
.BR xil\-init (1)
